History of this document
------------------------

2006/02/26 1.1  - updated with menu titles, hint by GGS (tokai)
2006/02/26 1.1  - updated for Assigns in "My MorphOS" (tokai)
2006/02/26 1.0  - first final draft (tokai)


The goals of this document
--------------------------

With current Ambient (26th February 2006) context menus have no design at
all, but are just a randomly put together bunch of the required actions.
This is not only confusing, but sometimes also frustrating for the user
when the menues are far away from usability (e.g. View and Show are very
confusing, happens not rarely you go to wrong menu first. This is Stop-
Energy would ChaoZer say ;).

The main idea of this very concept is that all actions which appear
somethere in the context menus follow a global order. So the small
part of the actions which appear in each sub context menu still appear
in the same order always. This is less confusing for the user and brings
more consistency to the desktop.

The second idea is that all actions in the global order are sorted
into logical groups sorted by priority of use. First default actions,
then actions, options and lastly selection and the cut/copy/paste
block (which are actions too, but very rarely used usually and not
really required as Copy/Move is usually done by just dragging the
icons to different destination directly on the desktop).

As 3rd idea Show/View gets merged into one submenu which is more
logical build up.


Advantages/ Disadvantages
-------------------------

Current system:  - no real uniform look (same options appear at different
                   places across the miscellanous menus)
                 - subitems appear not in logical order of priority
                   (so important stuff is at bottom, less important
                   at top, etc.)
                 - very confusing View/Show submenus

New system:      - more work :)
                 + uniform look across all submenus
                 + logical order of priority
                 + nice View submenu


The global design/ order
------------------------

  Menu                            Description
  ------------------------------
  Open                            ; default action (fileactions) or opens dir in current view (browser mode)
  Open...                         ; opens dir in new window (spatial mode)
  Open in new Window...           ; opens dir in new window (browser mode)
  Open Shell...
  Find...
  Actions >>   ....               ; submenu for other cutom actions
  ------------------------------
  Information...
  ------------------------------
  New Drawer...
  Rename...                       ; dots are not shown if actions doesn't popup the window (prefs)
  Put Away...
  Dismount...                     ; for Assigns in "My MorphOS", maybe misleading.. but thats opposite to "Assign" in DOS i think :)
  Delete...
  Format...
  ------------------------------
  View    >>   [x] as Icons       ; radio list
                   as List
               -----------------
               [x] All files      ; if activated all files are shown, else only files with an icon
               [x] Thumbnails     ; if activated it will show thumbnails for graphic files with no icon

  Sort    >>   [x] automaticaly   ; if deactivated manual sorting is possible (for later, maybe ;)
               ----------------
               [x] by Name        ; radio list
                   by Type
                   by Size
                   by Date
  -----------------------------
  Snapshot
  -----------------------------
  Select All
  Invert
  -----------------------------
  Cut                       
  Copy
  Paste
  Paste into                      ; takes currently selected drawer as paste target
  -----------------------------



The submenus
------------

Basic overview of all required context menues depending on place the
user clicked. Titles of the menues are between [ and ] at top of each
picture.


on a drawer icon:

    (spatial view)                   (browser view)

    [Directory]                      [Directory]
    ----------------------------     ----------------------------
    Open...                          Open
    Open Shell...                    Open in new Window...
    Find...                          Open Shell...
    ----------------------------     Find...
    Information...                   ----------------------------
    ----------------------------     Information...
    Rename...                        ----------------------------
    Delete...                        Rename...
    ----------------------------     Delete...
    Cut                              ----------------------------
    Copy                             Cut
    Paste into                       Copy
    ----------------------------     Paste into
                                     ----------------------------



inside drawer/device window:

    [Icons/List]¹
    ----------------------------
    Open Shell...
    Find...
    ----------------------------
    New Drawer...
    ----------------------------
    View                      >>   
    Sort                      >> 
    ----------------------------
    Snapshot
    ----------------------------
    Select All
    Invert
    ----------------------------
    Cut                       
    Copy
    Paste
    ----------------------------
    
    ¹) depending on current view, maybe just "Files" is enough. Currently it
    uses "Icons" for icon view and "Files" for list view.

  

on device icon in root window:

    (spatial view)                  (browser view)
    [Volume]                        [Volume]
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Open...                         Open...
    Open Shell...                   Open Shell...
    Find...                         Find...
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Information...                  Information...
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Rename...                       Rename...
    Put Away...                     Put Away...
    Format...                       Format...
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Paste into                      Paste into
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------

on device icon in "My MorphOS":

    (spatial view)                  (browser view)
    [Volume]                        [Volume]
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Open...                         Open
    Open Shell...                   Open in new Window...
    Find...                         Open Shell...
    ----------------------------    Find...
    Information...                  ----------------------------
    ----------------------------    Information...
    Rename...                       ----------------------------
    Put Away...                     Rename...
    Format...                       Put Away...
    ----------------------------    Format...
    Paste into                      ----------------------------
    ----------------------------    Paste into
                                    ----------------------------

on "My MorphOS" icon (root window):

    [My MorphOS]
    ----------------------------
    Open...
    Find...
    ----------------------------
    Put Away...
    ----------------------------


on "Assign" icon in "My MorphOS"¹:

    (spatial view)                  (browser view)
    [Assign]                        [Assign]
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Open...                         Open
    Open Shell...                   Open in new Window...
    Find...                         Open Shell...
    ----------------------------    Find...
    Dismount...                     ----------------------------
    ----------------------------    Dismount...
    Paste into                      ----------------------------
    ----------------------------    Paste into
                                    ----------------------------    

    ¹) no "Information" menu item , as it's missleading in this 
       context: get Information on Assign or the destination 
       directory?


on a file (with example actions)²:

    (without icon or default        (with icon and default
     tool)                           tool)
    [<filetype>]                    [<filetype>]
    ----------------------------    ----------------------------
    Open with Multiview...          Open with [Defaulttool]...¹
    Actions                   >>    Actions                   >>
        +----------------------+        +----------------------+
        | Edit with MorphED... |        | Open with Multiview..|
        | Compile with gcc     |        | Edit with MorphED... |
        +----------------------+        | Compile with gcc     |
    ----------------------------        +----------------------+
    Information...                  ----------------------------
    ----------------------------    Information
    Rename...                       ...
    Delete...
    ----------------------------
    Cut                       
    Copy
    ----------------------------

    ¹) [DefaultTool] == FilePart(DefaultTool) of course :)
    ²) Executables have no "actions" block. (needs input, as they could
       have possible Actions as "Open in HEX Editor" etc., so they maybe should
       have at least the "Actions >>" submenu).
